        "v": 5,
        "title": "Fix CONTRIBUTING.md and knowledge.md dev instructions",
        "summary": "Updated CONTRIBUTING.md and knowledge.md to remove the incorrect claim that `bun dev` runs both web and CLI. Clarified that `bun up` starts services, requiring separate execution of `bun start-cli` for the CLI. This aligns documentation with actual command behavior, removing Option A/B distinction in favor of explicit terminal steps.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T02:04:41.255Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The instructions for new contributors were corrected so they no longer claim a single command starts both the web interface and the command-line tool. You would notice this if you followed the guide: the old steps that promised one command would launch everything are gone, replaced by clear steps showing the web server must be started first, then the command-line tool in a second step. This affects anyone trying to set up a local development copy using the project's own guide.",
